[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Artifact flush mutation classification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARTIFACT-MUTANT-CLASSIFICATION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve raw outcomes and bound equivalent-mutant claims
STATEMENT: >>>
Mutation triage shall retain the original tool outcome and distinguish a
behavior-changing survivor from a platform/version-bounded equivalent mutation.
The LimitedFile::flush replacement with Ok(()) shall not be called killed when
the delegated unbuffered File::flush is a no-op. The explicit sync_all publication
steps shall remain intact. Reassess this classification when the writer,
standard library or target semantics change; do not exclude every future flush
mutation or infer power-loss durability from finite I/O probes.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Trace: src/artifact.rs flush and publish; experiments/file-flush.rs;
scripts/Probe-FileFlush.ps1; docs/artifact-flush-equivalence.md.
Bounded triage record: evidence/artifact-flush-triage.json. It is assessment data,
not a tool exclusion or an instruction to rewrite native outcomes.
Original run: 20261114T080050Z-eeffe372, issue47. Raw survivor count remains one.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARTIFACT-TEST-WORKDIR-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Separate coverage test working directory from source
STATEMENT: >>>
The Rust integration coverage helper shall accept and validate an explicit test
working directory before compilation, while retaining source-relative build
inputs. Tests with relative artifact paths shall be executable under the E:
artifact root without creating bulk output in the source checkout. Omitting the
option shall preserve existing callers' working-directory behavior.
<<<
